I now have a complete picture of every concrete type implementing `storage.Querier` across both repos. I have all the evidence needed for a thorough analysis. Let me now write the comprehensive answer.

---

## 1. Architecture Overview

The `Querier` interface lives in `storage/interface.go` in the **prometheus** repo and is the **central read contract** for all time-series data access. Every component that evaluates PromQL — from the TSDB engine itself, to Mimir's query-frontend, to remote-read handlers — obtains a `Querier` and calls its methods.

The current interface (lines 122–132) is:

```go
// Querier provides querying access over time series data of a fixed time range.
type Querier interface {
    LabelQuerier                                                          // LabelValues, LabelNames, Close

    Select(ctx context.Context, sortSeries bool, hints *SelectHints,
           matchers ...*labels.Matcher) SeriesSet
}
```

Adding `SelectSorted` introduces a **second, always-sorted selection path** alongside `Select`. Because Go interfaces are satisfied **structurally and implicitly**, every concrete type that currently satisfies `Querier` will **immediately fail to compile** until it also implements `SelectSorted`. The blast radius spans two repos — **prometheus** and **mimir** — with every wrapper, adapter, mock, and decorator needing a new method body.

The end-to-end query path that touches `Querier` is:

```
PromQL Engine / Streaming Engine
        │  calls Queryable.Querier(mint, maxt)
        ▼
  storage.Querier  ◄──── NEW: SelectSorted() must be added here
        │  calls Select() / SelectSorted()
        ▼
  storage.SeriesSet  (iterated by engine)
```

---

## 2. Detailed Analysis

### 2.1 The Interface Definition — `storage/interface.go` (prometheus)

**File:** `storage/interface.go`, lines 122–132

```go
type Querier interface {
    LabelQuerier
    Select(ctx context.Context, sortSeries bool,
           hints *SelectHints, matchers ...*labels.Matcher) SeriesSet
}
```

The new method to add:

```go
SelectSorted(ctx context.Context, hints *SelectHints,
             matchers ...*labels.Matcher) SeriesSet
```

`SelectHints` is defined at lines 203–250 of the same file. `SeriesSet` is defined at lines 412–424. The `MockQuerier` struct at lines 134–153 also implements `Querier` and must gain a `SelectSorted` stub.

---

### 2.2 Prometheus Repo — All Concrete `Querier` Implementors

#### `storage/noop.go` — `noopQuerier`
```go
type noopQuerier struct{}
func (noopQuerier) Select(context.Context, bool, *SelectHints, ...*labels.Matcher) SeriesSet {
    return NoopSeriesSet()
}
```
**Required addition:**
```go
func (noopQuerier) SelectSorted(context.Context, *SelectHints, ...*labels.Matcher) SeriesSet {
    return NoopSeriesSet()
}
```

#### `storage/merge.go` — `querierAdapter` (wraps `mergeGenericQuerier`)
`NewMergeQuerier` (line 46) returns a `*querierAdapter` which delegates to `mergeGenericQuerier.Select`. The `querierAdapter.Select` at line 91 calls `q.genericQuerier.Select(ctx, sortSeries, hints, matchers...)`. A `SelectSorted` implementation would call `q.genericQuerier.Select(ctx, true, hints, matchers...)` — i.e., always pass `sortSeries=true`.

#### `storage/secondary.go` — `secondaryQuerier` (wraps `genericQuerier`)
`secondaryQuerier.Select` at line 68 records async sets and wraps them in a `lazyGenericSeriesSet`. A `SelectSorted` would do the same but always pass `sortSeries=true` to the inner `genericQuerier.Select`.

#### `storage/generic.go` — `querierAdapter`
The `querierAdapter.Select` at line 91 is the concrete `Querier`-facing method. It must gain a `SelectSorted` that calls `q.genericQuerier.Select(ctx, true, hints, matchers...)`.

