### 2.3 Mimir Repo — All Concrete `storage.Querier` Implementors

#### `pkg/storage/lazyquery/lazyquery.go` — `LazyQuerier`
```go
func (l LazyQuerier) Select(ctx context.Context, selectSorted bool,
    params *storage.SelectHints, matchers ...*labels.Matcher) storage.SeriesSet {
    future := make(chan storage.SeriesSet, 1)
    copiedParams := copyParams(params)
    go func() {
        future <- l.next.Select(ctx, selectSorted, copiedParams, matchers...)
    }()
    return &lazySeriesSet{future: future}
}
```
**Required addition:**
```go
func (l LazyQuerier) SelectSorted(ctx context.Context,
    params *storage.SelectHints, matchers ...*labels.Matcher) storage.SeriesSet {
    future := make(chan storage.SeriesSet, 1)
    copiedParams := copyParams(params)
    go func() {
        future <- l.next.SelectSorted(ctx, copiedParams, matchers...)
    }()
    return &lazySeriesSet{future: future}
}
```

#### `pkg/querier/blocks_store_queryable.go` — `blocksStoreQuerier`
```go
// Select implements storage.Querier interface.
// The bool passed is ignored because the series is always sorted.
func (q *blocksStoreQuerier) Select(ctx context.Context, _ bool,
    sp *storage.SelectHints, matchers ...*labels.Matcher) storage.SeriesSet {
    tenantID, err := tenant.TenantID(ctx)
    ...
    return q.selectSorted(ctx, sp, tenantID, matchers...)
}
```
Note: the comment says "the bool passed is ignored because the series is always sorted." `SelectSorted` is a natural fit here — it would simply call `q.selectSorted(...)` directly without the ignored bool.

**Required addition:**
```go
func (q *blocksStoreQuerier) SelectSorted(ctx context.Context,
    sp *storage.SelectHints, matchers ...*labels.Matcher) storage.SeriesSet {
    tenantID, err := tenant.TenantID(ctx)
    if err != nil {
        return storage.ErrSeriesSet(err)
    }
    return q.selectSorted(ctx, sp, tenantID, matchers...)
}
```

